      "key_excerpt": "Distributed tensor computation is an orthogonal and more general approach that partitions a tensor operation across multiple devices to accelerate computation or increase model size. [...] In this work, we implement a simple and efficient model parallel approach using intra-layer model-parallelism. [...] for the self attention block we exploit inherent parallelism in the multihead attention operation, partitioning the GEMMs associated with key (K), query (Q), and value (V) in a column parallel fashion such that the matrix multiply corresponding to each attention head is done locally on one GPU [...] Our model parallelism is primarily designed to enable training models larger than what can fit in the memory of a single GPU [...] We illustrate this approach by converging transformer based models up to 8.3 billion parameters using 512 GPUs.",
